+# Build Scalariform with Hindi keywords for Kojo
+
+## Source and scope
+
+- Clone origin: https://github.com/bulent2k2/scalariform.git
+- Baseline: commit `8cf96a69d7a87a4b4d31a4061b8eb1ca615fd896`, Scalariform 0.2.10,
+  immediately before that fork's Turkish keyword additions.
+- Checkout: pinned upstream baseline with the Hindi patch applied; a detached HEAD is supported.
+- Added aliases: `मान` = `VAL`, `चर` = `VAR`, `परिभाषा` = `DEF`, `यदि` = `IF`, `अन्यथा` = `ELSE`.
+- The English entries remain. Turkish aliases are not included in this Hindi build.
+
+Only `scalariform/src/main/scala/scalariform/lexer/Keywords.scala` needs a language
+change. Existing token types, parser, and formatting rules are reused, preserving
+Hindi source text rather than translating it back to English.
+
+The reference instructions are:
+- https://github.com/bulent2k2/scalariform/blob/master/README_bulent2k2
+- https://github.com/bulent2k2/scalariform/blob/master/Makefile
+- https://github.com/bulent2k2/scalariform/commit/f79bb1dbd46cb51874845333b65bec6e100cd623
+
+## Build definition and prerequisites
+
+The upstream root build uses sbt 1.2.8 and obsolete publishing/assembly plugins.
+An attempt to build it could not resolve four of those plugins from Maven Central.
+For repeatable library builds, use the added `hi-build/` sbt project. It compiles
+the original library and test sources with:
+
+- sbt 1.11.7 and Scala 2.13.18, targeting Java 8 bytecode;
+- the original runtime modules: scala-xml 1.2.0 and scala-parser-combinators 1.1.2;
+- stable ScalaTest 3.0.8 for the existing FlatSpec/Matchers test suite;
+- no publishing, formatting-on-compile, or assembly plugins.
+
+The resulting library version is `0.2.10-hi`. The dedicated build is intended
+for Kojo's plain JVM classpath; it does not reproduce the upstream OSGi manifest,
+CLI assembly, publishing configuration, or generated BuildInfo object.
+The original upstream build files remain untouched.
+
+Use the sibling `../tools/sbt` launcher. It defaults to `java` on PATH and was
+tested here with AdoptOpenJDK 1.8.0_265. Optionally set `KOJO_HI_JAVA` to a Java
+executable. Build the sibling Scala checkout first so its patched jars are
+available for the final integration check.
+
+## Build and verify
+
+Prepare the workspace using [the shared recipe](../README.md). These commands
+use its `workspace` variable; in a new shell set it to the printed absolute path.
+
+```bash
+cd "$workspace/scala"
+./build-hi.sh
+cd ../scalariform
+./build-hi.sh
+```
+
+The Scalariform script runs:
+
+```bash
+cd hi-build
+../../tools/sbt test packageBin stageRuntimeDependencies
+```
+
+The two runtime modules are staged under
+`hi-build/target/runtime-dependencies/`, outside the release artifacts. Kojo
+already depends on these module versions. The verification script uses those
+modules, the built formatter jar and the sibling Scala distribution directly.
+
+After the checks pass, `../tools/package-release.py` stages exactly four jars,
+`SHA256SUMS` and `LICENSES.zip` in `../artifacts/`. Checksums cover only the four
+release jars. The license archive is collected from the Scala and Scalariform
+source checkouts and includes the upstream license, NOTICE and third-party
+license texts. No dependency jars or documentation are staged in `artifacts/`.
+See [the release packaging instructions](../README.md#package-and-publish-release-assets)
+for the release file list.
+
+Run only the library tests:
+
+```bash
+(cd "$workspace/scalariform/hi-build" && ../../tools/sbt test)
+```
+
+Run only the new Hindi tests:
+
+```bash
+(cd "$workspace/scalariform/hi-build" && ../../tools/sbt 'testOnly scalariform.lexer.HindiKeywordsTest')
+```
+
+Run the built-jar integration check after building Scala and staging formatter dependencies:
+
+```bash
+(cd "$workspace/scalariform" && ./verify-hi.sh)
+```
+
+`HindiKeywordsTest` checks token types, source offsets and exact Hindi spelling,
+longer identifiers, backquoted identifiers, comments and strings, mixed English
+and Hindi formatting, conditional forms with mixed English/Hindi keywords,
+and formatting idempotence. The jar integration check
+formats the sibling compiler's smoke-test source, then compiles and runs that
+formatted source with the built Hindi compiler. The test output is kept under
+`hi-tests/target/`.
+
+## Outputs
+
+- Primary library: `hi-build/target/scala-2.13/scalariform.jar`.
+- Ready-to-use copy: `../artifacts/scalariform.jar`.
+- Runtime modules for local verification: `hi-build/target/runtime-dependencies/`.
+- Other release files: three matching Scala jars, `SHA256SUMS` and `LICENSES.zip`.
+- Artifact documentation: [the shared recipe](../README.md#package-and-publish-release-assets).
+- Combined build and verification log: `../logs/build.log`.
+
+Kojo's Hindi toolchain uses this `scalariform.jar` with all three matching Hindi
+Scala jars. These scripts stage the files in this workspace; provisioning a
+Kojo installation is a separate step described in the `scala-indic` repository
+README.
+
+## Verified result
+
+The complete `build-hi.sh` run succeeded on Java 1.8.0_265: 1,021 tests
+passed across 40 suites, with 4 upstream tests pending. The staged-jar
+format/compile/run integration check passed.
